---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="Privacy notes for this template. Edit them before you publish. This is not legal advice."
>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <aside class="edit-callout">
    <p>
      <strong>Edit this page before you publish.</strong> It is a starting point, not legal advice, and it is not a
      claim that any ad network has approved the site. The file is <code>src/pages/privacy.astro</code>.
    </p>
  </aside>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Who publishes this</h2>
    <p>
      Replace this with your name and how to reach you. The template author field currently says “{site.author}”.
      Do not invent an email address.
    </p>
    <h2>What this template does</h2>
    <p>
      The pages are built ahead of time from Markdown files. There is no account, no sign-in, and no database. The
      template does not ship an analytics script or an advertising script.
    </p>
    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      When you turn on GitHub Pages, GitHub serves the built files. This page does not describe GitHub’s own privacy
      terms. Read those on GitHub and change this section if you host the files somewhere else.
    </p>
    <h2>Public repository</h2>
    <p>
      If the GitHub repository is public, the Markdown files, drafts, and media are public even when
      <code>draft: true</code> keeps a tutorial off the built site. Do not commit secrets or private pictures.
    </p>
    <h2>YouTube</h2>
    <p>
      A tutorial loads a player from <code>youtube-nocookie.com</code> only when that tutorial’s file includes a
      video link. YouTube’s policies apply to that player. Delete the link to remove the player.
    </p>
    <h2>Ads</h2>
    <p>
      <code>ads.enabled</code> is {site.ads.enabled ? 'true' : 'false'}. While it is false, no ad slot is shown and no
      publisher ID is included. This template does not claim approval from any ad network. If you later paste your
      own ad snippet, rewrite this section and keep only an ID that belongs to you.
    </p>
    <h2>Search</h2>
    <p>
      The archive filter runs in the visitor’s browser on a list built with the site. It is not sent to a search
      company by this template.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
